Done. Implemented P5.1 chat realtime fan-out (slice: P5.1 bullet 3).

**What I did**
- New listener `chat-realtime.listener.ts` consumes `chatMessage`/`chatReaction`/`chatReadCursor` database events (metadata engine owns the CRUD, so no second socket path).
- New `ChatRealtimePublisherService` publishes `chat.message.created|updated|deleted`, `chat.reaction.created|deleted`, `chat.read.updated` via `RealtimePublisherService.publish(buildChatChannelTopic(...))` — `workspace:<id>:chat:<channelId>`.
- Read events carry an aggregated unread count (`chat-unread-count.util.ts`), with the durable `chatReadCursor.lastReadAt` as the cursor — never a per-socket seq.
- Pure event builders (`chat-realtime-event.util.ts`); reaction channel resolved from `chatMessage`; unread aggregated under system context.
- Registered providers in `chat.module.ts`.

